 C/RR:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C C/RR - load a non-simple packed field (a packed array element, or an
C MSB-ordered struct) addressed through a pointer.
C
C   Entry:  ACC = the field's shift amount (untagged plain integer)
C           M11 = address of the width-specific table (C/01/C/02/C/03/
C                 C/04/C/06/C/07, picked by work.p2c at compile time --
C                 see libc/c_01.madlen)
C           M14 = address of the word(s) containing the field, set by
C                 setAddrTo(14)
C           M13 = return link
C
C prepLoad (work.p2c) selects this over C/LDAR when the value's kind is
C a packed array, or a struct not declared __lsb.  Shares C/LDAR's
C prologue; diverges only in the final extraction.  This is a verbatim
C port of the Pascal runtime's P/RR (paslib/p_rr.dtran); the width-table
C format it reads via M11 is not independently understood beyond the
C shape documented at c_01.madlen.  The fixpoint check and full test
C suite verify it (test 30 reaches this specific routine).
C===========================================================
                ,NTR ,3
            1   ,AOX ,11B
           15   ,ATX ,1
           11   ,A*X ,
                ,ATI ,10
           10   ,J+M ,14
           11   ,A*X ,1
                ,YTA ,100B
           15   ,X-A ,1
                ,ATI ,10
           14   ,XTA ,
           10   ,UTC ,
           11   ,ASX ,5
           11   ,WTC ,3
                ,ASX ,-2
                ,YTA ,
           13   ,UJ  ,
                ,END ,
